  <section id="install" class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Install in a minute</h2>
      <p>On Debian/Ubuntu with the apt repository (one build per PHP minor; replace <code>8.1</code> with yours). The key is pinned to this repo only:</p>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>sudo install -d -m 0755 /etc/apt/keyrings
curl -fsSL https://howdah.org/key.asc | sudo tee /etc/apt/keyrings/howdah.asc &gt;/dev/null
echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/howdah.asc] {PKG}/apt stable main" \
  | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/howdah.list
sudo apt-get update &amp;&amp; sudo apt-get install php8.1-howdah</code></pre>
      <p>On RHEL/CentOS/Alma (Remi layout) the package is <code>php81-howdah</code> via <code>yum</code>, with both package and metadata signatures enforced. Both package names, the exact <code>.repo</code> file, the signed-tarball path for other setups, and the verify/rollback steps are in the picker. Once it is installed, the config editor writes your <code>howdah.ini</code> and <code>howdah.toml</code> from a form and checks the TOML with the extension's own parser.</p>
      <p><a class="btn primary" href="/install/">Open the install picker</a> <a class="btn ghost" href="/config/">Build your config file</a> <a class="btn ghost" href="/coverage/">Check your PHP version first</a></p>
    </div>
